      "startedAt": 1792847349177,
      "finishedAt": 1792847349179,
      "exitCode": 1,
      "diagnostic": "<Contract id=\"ENTITY_INVENTORY_FORMAT\">\n  `AX_SPEC_TABLE_IS_INDEX` (v2, `shared/sdd/check.ts`): a table is an index, not text — `Purpose` is\n  one short line (checked: ≤120 chars, one sentence, no `<br>`); anything longer moves to that\n  entity's `### <EntityName>` block in Entity Surfaces, not into this cell.\n\n  ```markdown\n  ## Entity Inventory\n\n  _Это полный список сущностей модуля. Любое введение сущности execution-агентом помимо этого списка считается drift'ом и требует обновления spec._\n\n  | Name | Type | Purpose |\n  |------|------|---------|\n  | `OrderProcessor` | Service | Композитная обработка lifecycle заказа |\n  | `PaymentGatewayPort` | Port | Абстракция для списания средств |\n  | `StripePaymentAdapter` | Adapter | Реализация PaymentGatewayPort через Stripe |\n  | `RefundLedger` | Service | Учёт возвратов — Deferred Implementation: INP-rel-dep |\n  ```\n\n  **`Deferred Implementation: <TSK-id>`** — a declared entity whose build is deliberately owned\n  by a FUTURE ticket, not this module's current Round. Append it to that row's `Purpose` cell (or\n  to a bullet-row's tail, same style as `Deferred Test Ownership:` in Test Scenario Coverage): the\n  entity may exist in this Inventory with no code behind it yet without being drift. `gennady\n  lint --spec=<spec> --inventory-reverse <code-root>` reads the marker and reports that row as an\n  informational line, never `ERR_CLI_LINT_INVENTORY_UNIMPLEMENTED` — the reverse sweep still\n  flags every OTHER declared-but-unbuilt entity as drift exactly as before.\n\n  **Errors ownership is first-class**, not an afterthought: either one row above is the explicit\n  errors owner (its `Purpose` says so, e.g. «Владеет обработкой/показом ошибок платежа»), or the\n  inventory carries one extra line right under the table:\n\n  ```markdown\n  Ошибки: <механизм — throw | Result | event | …> → <владелец: EntityName>\n  ```\n\n  A BDD ticket downstream cannot require behavior on an error whose owner is absent from this\n  inventory — that gap is caught here, before approval, not discovered later at scaffold time.\n\n  **ER sketch — mandatory once ≥2 entities are relationally connected** (one references, owns,\n  or is composed of another): the table alone shows WHAT exists, not HOW the entities relate,\n  and a relationship among ≥2 elements is exactly the case a picture beats a paragraph\n  (`AX_INFOGRAPHIC_FIRST`, `formats/diagram-vocabulary.xml`). Add it directly under the table:\n\n  ```markdown\n  Order ──1:N──▶ OrderLine\n    - id (PK)      - id (PK)\n    - customerId   - orderId (FK)\n  ```\n\n  A single-entity inventory (nothing to relate) or a set of genuinely unrelated entities skips\n  the sketch — state which case applies, never leave the reader guessing. This ASCII form is\n  shown in chat during the STEP_2_ENTITY_INVENTORY interview, at the point the entities and\n  their relations are confirmed (`AX_CHAT_BEFORE_SPEC`); the mermaid `erDiagram` version below\n  the table is the same shape, not a fresh diagram invented at write time.\n</Contract>\nzsh:1: === not found\n",
